---
// C-020 — the site is dark only, so this override renders nothing at all.
//
// Starlight's own ThemeProvider ships one inline, before-paint script that
// reads `localStorage.getItem('starlight-theme')`, falls back to
// `prefers-color-scheme`, and writes the result to
// `document.documentElement.dataset.theme`. Replacing it with nothing is what
// makes the site dark-only, and it is enough on its own: Starlight's
// `Page.astro` already renders `data-theme="dark"` into the served HTML
// (`htmlDataAttributes` there is a hardcoded literal), so removing the script
// leaves the attribute standing with nothing able to change it — no flash, no
// stored preference, no `prefers-color-scheme` read.
//
// Re-emitting the attribute here would be the redundant half; dropping the
// script is the whole change. There is no config flag for dark-only, which is
// why this is a component override rather than a setting.
//
// It also defined `window.StarlightThemeProvider`, whose only callers are in
// `ThemeSelect.astro` — overridden to render nothing beside this. Nothing else
// in the package references the global.
---
